# Generated from: specs/227-build-the-ue-compile-gate-with-the-default-toolchain-again-drop-nouba/requirements.md
Feature: gate-ue-compile builds with the default UE 5.8 toolchain

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: The gate passes the default arguments to Build.sh
    Given a fake Build.sh under UE_ROOT that logs its arguments
    And a project at fixtures/dogfood.uproject
    When the project.ue-compile provider compiles target DogfoodEditor
    Then Build.sh receives DogfoodEditor, Mac, Development, -Project=<absolute project path> and -WaitMutex
    And it does not receive -NoUBA

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The documented gate row describes the default build
    Given steering/snippets/project-tech.md
    When the gate-ue-compile row is read
    Then it contains "Build.sh DogfoodEditor Mac Development -WaitMutex"
    And it does not mention -NoUBA, the Unreal Build Accelerator, or parallel worktrees

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The unit test rejects a build that passes -NoUBA
    Given tests/unit/test_ue_compile_gate.py and the fake Build.sh
    When the test runs the provider
    Then it asserts the exact default argument list
    And it asserts that -NoUBA is absent from the logged arguments and from the command evidence

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The headless master-material build uses the default toolchain
    Given a fake UE engine under UE_ROOT whose Build.sh logs its arguments
    When scripts/unreal/build_master_material.py --headless builds DogfoodEditor
    Then Build.sh receives DogfoodEditor, Mac, Development, -Project=<dogfood project> and -WaitMutex
    And it does not receive -NoUBA
